+## Storage and administration
 
-Stable entry IDs are SHA-256 of the complete canonical language-prefixed string. java: and java-source: retain source-spelled owners/types; aidl: retains AIDL descriptors and source member signatures; jvm: retains published binary owners and JVM method descriptors (field types may be absent from the lifecycle index). Every language uses the package: infix for package declarations where present. These four namespaces are distinct until explicit equivalence is proven; spelling changes can change source IDs and never silently retarget grants. The full forms and minor-version vocabulary are listed below. A declaration revision is its canonical JSON SHA-256, scoped by immutable source ID and locator; changes in permission metadata do not overwrite earlier declarations. Current entry ETags use the single cat1 formula in API-CONTRACT.md, including current registry generation, base hash, identity, overlay revision and state. All source occurrences and their potentially different permissions remain available. Conflicting or source-dependent permission expressions produce an unknown aggregate rather than an invented union or intersection.
